WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.520
- Well, there's a recall
election for governor coming here

00:00:03.520 --> 00:00:06.147
and a friend of yours,
Caitlyn Jenner is running.

00:00:06.147 --> 00:00:08.640
So does that make it easier or harder

00:00:08.640 --> 00:00:09.860
to decide who to support?

00:00:09.860 --> 00:00:11.260
Because I know in all seriousness

00:00:11.260 --> 00:00:13.640
it's a completely different
job than when you were acting

00:00:13.640 --> 00:00:15.710
and it's a big undertaking you know?

00:00:15.710 --> 00:00:17.170
And it's a lot of work.

00:00:17.170 --> 00:00:19.110
So is it hard for you when it's a friend

00:00:19.110 --> 00:00:20.627
or is it easier for you to be like,

00:00:20.627 --> 00:00:22.370
"No, I'm gonna cut the crap,
I'm gonna tell you this."

00:00:22.370 --> 00:00:24.340
Like is it easy or hard for you?

00:00:24.340 --> 00:00:26.200
- Well, it's not easy or hard.

00:00:26.200 --> 00:00:28.640
It makes no difference
to me because the fact

00:00:28.640 --> 00:00:32.050
of the matter is, is that
I stay out of the race.

00:00:32.050 --> 00:00:33.290
As I've said many times.

00:00:33.290 --> 00:00:36.920
I said that Gavin Newsome
is a friend of mine.

00:00:36.920 --> 00:00:38.420
Caitlin is a friend of mine, a lot

00:00:38.420 --> 00:00:41.208
of other people that may
run and will announce

00:00:41.208 --> 00:00:44.240
are friends of mine but
I don't get involved

00:00:44.240 --> 00:00:48.120
because, you know I have the
USC Schwarzenegger Institute,

00:00:48.120 --> 00:00:49.893
which is a bipartisan institute,

00:00:50.850 --> 00:00:52.610
kinda like a think tank in a way.

00:00:52.610 --> 00:00:55.360
We talk about various important issues

00:00:55.360 --> 00:00:58.870
of healthcare, infrastructure,
environmental issues

00:00:58.870 --> 00:01:00.960
homeless issues, and so on and so forth.

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:03.590
So the only way you really
can do that successfully

00:01:03.590 --> 00:01:06.380
is if you're able to bring
Democrats and Republicans

00:01:06.380 --> 00:01:09.900
to the experts in the various
different subjects together.

00:01:09.900 --> 00:01:11.700
And so therefore I don't
want to get involved

00:01:11.700 --> 00:01:14.100
in a political arena at all.

00:01:14.100 --> 00:01:16.950
I don't to support Democrats
or to support Republicans.

00:01:16.950 --> 00:01:18.220
But I said, I stay out of it.

00:01:18.220 --> 00:01:20.730
- I think that's really
important, that think tank.

00:01:20.730 --> 00:01:22.810
That's a really important, I mean,

00:01:22.810 --> 00:01:25.000
on a global level, I
think that's important

00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:26.610
that no matter what our beliefs are,

00:01:26.610 --> 00:01:28.130
no matter what your principles,

00:01:28.130 --> 00:01:29.750
that the core thing is that everyone wants

00:01:29.750 --> 00:01:31.830
to be happy and healthy.

00:01:31.830 --> 00:01:33.640
You wanna be able to get your kids healthy

00:01:33.640 --> 00:01:36.190
and get, you know,
healthcare and, and all that.

00:01:36.190 --> 00:01:38.520
So I think that that think tank idea is,

00:01:38.520 --> 00:01:40.570
that's what really needs
to happen regardless

00:01:40.570 --> 00:01:43.553
of what political side
of the fence you land on.

